{"id":"cost-per-home","title":"What a subsidized home costs to build","tier":"REDFLAG","question":"What does each City-backed affordable home cost in total, by developer, and how has that moved?","finding":"61 San Francisco developments in State tax-credit staff reports from 2018 to 2026 budget $5,950,063,584 for 7,158 homes. New-build cost per home has a middle value of $943,615; the middle rose from $750,174 in 2018 to $976,163 in 2026. The dearest is Sunnydale HOPE SF Block 7 at $1,203,262 a home.","how":"Total project cost and homes from the “Project Cost Summary at Application” in each California Tax Credit Allocation Committee staff report on disk (2018 onward), by the year in the application number. “Against the middle” compares with the middle new-build cost per home across all years. Warning signs counts flags this site already holds against the developer.","limits":"These are budgets at application, not audited final costs; only 61 of 289 San Francisco tax-credit projects have a staff report with costs on disk. Cost per home depends on unit size, building height, land, parking, commercial space and prevailing-wage rules, so high cost is not waste by itself. Totals include land and financing.","columns":[{"k":"project","t":"Development","type":"text"},{"k":"developer","t":"Developer","type":"org"},{"k":"year","t":"Year","type":"year"},{"k":"kind","t":"Kind","type":"text"},{"k":"homes","t":"Homes","type":"int"},{"k":"totalCost","t":"Total cost","type":"usd"},{"k":"perHome","t":"Cost per home","type":"usd"},{"k":"timesMedian","t":"Against the middle","type":"times"},{"k":"developerFee","t":"Developer fee","type":"usd"},{"k":"warningSigns","t":"Warning signs elsewhere","type":"int"},{"k":"file","t":"Staff report","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"project":"Sunnydale HOPE SF Block 7","address":"65 Santos Street","developer":"Mercy Housing California","developerKey":"MERCY HOUSING CALIFORNIA","year":"2024","kind":"New Construction","homes":89,"totalCost":107090280,"perH